    {
      "id": "claim_8777da6eafe34452ad7d5c2d41521846",
      "statement": "Approval state is memory-only: pending actions and session grants live in the extension background and are cleared on bridge disconnect, extension reload, or session end (nothing persisted to localStorage, extension storage, or IndexedDB). approve_session is scoped to {origin, actionType} keyed origin\\u0000actionType, with the active tab origin re-checked before execution (a change yields approval_origin_changed). Approval timeout is application-level (default 55000ms, the HTTP timeout minus a buffer) returning approval_timeout; batch denial returns approval_denied for that action's actionUUID and continues, while timeout returns a partial batch_result. Approval error codes are approval_denied, approval_timeout, approval_unavailable, and approval_origin_changed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L139-L368",
