    {
      "id": "claim_2a1d66f6fd0d48bd801429ab24178921",
      "statement": "ADR 0061 requires the MCP server to forward the original error code and message rather than collapsing unknown codes into generics. parseRouterErrorEnvelope forwards any string code/message from a {type:'error'} envelope and only returns invalidResponse() when the envelope structure itself is malformed; parseErrorPayload preserves stale_context and page_navigated with their StaleContextDetail and forwards any other string code from the extension instead of wrapping it as browser_error. BrijioResourceResult/BrijioToolResult use code:string rather than the constrained union because the extension and WS server may emit codes the MCP server does not know.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0061-forward-error-codes-through-mcp.md#L69-L109",
