      "statement": "BrowserCapability is a closed union the extension advertises in BrowserPresence.capabilities: page_context, page_content, click, fill_input, fill_editable, set_checked, select_options, submit_form, navigate, batch, upload_file, download_status, download_file, fetch_resource, screenshot. isBrowserCapability is the validator used by the presence announce guard; the MCP server's BrowserPresence mirror keeps capabilities:string[] and required connectedAt/lastSeenAt but wire-time validation of capability strings lives in the shared package.",
